atlas forms

architecture form-graph
  canonical_name FormGraph
  family forms
  domain Forms
  layer forms
  semantic_question What is the structure of this human-boundary form, independent of any one submission?
  purpose The form as a graph -- fields, dependencies, evidence slots, attachments, approvals -- distinct from AtomicForm, which compiles it against state.
  maturity architectural
  node_types FormNode
  node_types FieldNode
  child form-attachment
  child field-dynamics
  edge_types field_depends_on
  forbidden_inference AtomicForm == FormGraph
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document
  known_gap FormGraph decomposition not yet built; AtomicForm exists standalone

architecture atomic-form
  canonical_name AtomicForm
  family forms
  domain Forms
  layer forms/compile
  semantic_question Is this form submit-ready, and if not, exactly what blocks it?
  purpose compile(FormGraph, institutional/actor/evidence/capability/economic/authority state, purpose) -> obligation machine. Fields autofill only from VERIFIED actors; never self-submits.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Field
  node_types EvidenceSlot
  node_types SubmitReadiness
  edge_types autofills_from
  edge_types backed_by
  invariant a field autofills only from a VERIFIED actor
  invariant submit_ready returns exact blockers; never a false green
  invariant the form never crosses the human submit line
  forbidden_inference asserted-via-email actor -> verified_for(profile) autofill
  forbidden_inference evidence slot filled by position -> evidence requirement satisfied
  command BonfyreBrief
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/atomic_forms.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/institution_loop.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_atomic_forms.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_institution_loop.py
  source_lineage AtomicForm human-boundary compiler
